Z||000003||Rob||02-20-2000||11:21 AM||||  The dash is a Pontiac Grand Prix. The side pod is from Auto Meter, they make them in both single and dual to fit 2" gauges.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||02-20-2000||12:34 PM||||Huh.  Someone else on the net must have thought it was as interesting as I did.  I got it off of the net, but not from RSMs site.  I wonder what you get for $59US?  Just the gauges?  (Not for me.)  Surely not the entire dash.  Wonder what it would take to modify the dash for the Fiero?  No way it would fit just like that without major trimming/modification.  Or could it?  I think an email to RSM is in order.<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 02-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||02-20-2000||03:14 PM||||I parked next to an mid 90s model Cavalier a few days ago, and I had some time to look in it while my sister went into a store. All black, not as angular as the late 80s/early 90s models, but it wasn't as rounded as the newer ones. My guess would be that it was a 1994-1996 Z24, but I'm not sure. (about the year I mean)<P>The dash looked pretty cool, somewhat similar in shape to the Grand Prix one pictured above.<P>Does anyone have any photos of the cavalier dashes to compare them?||||reg||1
